# Environment for throne-web.service, the web UI (EnvironmentFile=-/etc/throne/web.env). The unit is shipped disabled:
#   sudo systemctl enable --now throne-web
# Everything is commented out: the defaults need no entry. Uncomment a line to override it, then run
#   sudo systemctl restart throne-web
# A command-line flag wins over its variable; thronectl help web lists both. Never put the API key or a password here.
#
# The first start creates a password and logs it once:
#   sudo journalctl -u throne-web | grep 'web UI password'
# Change it in the web UI (System), or as root, which leaves the file to the unit's dynamic user; a running web UI
# picks it up within 5 seconds and signs every session out:
#   sudo thronectl web passwd --state-dir /var/lib/throne-web
#
# The unit runs as a dynamic user, which cannot read root-only files: they go in through LoadCredential=, as Throne's
# key /var/lib/throne/config/api.key does. For a key elsewhere (THRONE_API_KEY_FILE in throne.env), run
# sudo systemctl edit throne-web and add
#   [Service]
#   LoadCredential=
#   LoadCredential=api.key:/etc/throne/api.key

# Listen address: PORT, IPv4:PORT, [IPv6]:PORT, or *:PORT for every address. Default: 127.0.0.1:9096, this host only.
# A port below 1024 needs CAP_NET_BIND_SERVICE in AmbientCapabilities= and CapabilityBoundingSet= (systemctl edit).
#THRONE_WEB_LISTEN=*:9096

# HTTPS: auto, on or off. auto turns it on for a listen address other than loopback, with a self-signed certificate
# whose SHA-256 fingerprint the journal shows. Use off on a network address only behind a TLS reverse proxy.
#THRONE_WEB_TLS=auto

# Your own certificate chain and key (PEM) instead of the self-signed one. A root-only key goes in through
# LoadCredential=tls.key:/etc/ssl/private/throne.key (systemctl edit throne-web) and this path:
#THRONE_WEB_TLS_CERT=/etc/ssl/certs/throne.pem
#THRONE_WEB_TLS_KEY=/run/credentials/throne-web.service/tls.key

# Host names the browser may use, separated by commas. Needed for a name other than localhost on the default
# loopback listener, such as behind a reverse proxy; on a network address it limits the Host header to these names,
# loopback names and IP addresses.
#THRONE_WEB_ALLOW_HOST=throne.lan

# Throne API address, when Throne listens elsewhere (THRONE_API_LISTEN in throne.env). Default: 127.0.0.1:9095.
#THRONE_ADDR=192.168.1.2:9095

# Plain-text password file instead of the stored hash; the web UI and thronectl web passwd cannot change it then.
# A root-only file goes in through LoadCredential=web.password:/etc/throne/web.password and this path:
#THRONE_WEB_PASSWORD_FILE=/run/credentials/throne-web.service/web.password
